Keep the numeric-accumulation rule's braces in one row (dict-iteration.tex).
The rule of Syntax for the loop keyword `numeric-accumulation' sets a
\curly group over dict-iteration.tex:622-625, but a row break, \CR, at 623
ends the first table row inside the group, so the group opens in one cell
and closes in another, and \xcurly (a spacer as wide as the opening brace)
indents the continuation.  Drop the \CR and the spacer: the group is one
braced alternation, as the first group of the list-accumulation rule above it is.  The
printed rule loses its line break and its row may be wider; the line count
is unchanged.
--- dict-iteration.tex
+++ dict-iteration.tex
@@ -620,8 +620,8 @@
  \brac{\loopref{into} \param{simple-var}}}
 \auxbnf{numeric-accumulation}%
 {\curly{\loopref{count}    | \loopref{counting}   |
-	\loopref{sum}      | \loopref{summing}    | \CR
- \xcurly\loopref{maximize} | \loopref{maximizing} |
+	\loopref{sum}      | \loopref{summing}    |
+ \loopref{maximize} | \loopref{maximizing} |
         \loopref{minimize} | \loopref{minimizing}} \curly{\param{form} | \loopref{it}} \CR
  \brac{\loopref{into} \param{simple-var}} \brac{\param{type-spec}}}
 \auxbnf{conditional}%
